0" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & ={e}^{3x} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =1 \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =x{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f49b5b4-a291-5bee-8bd7-1b334e3bbe1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503067} {:answer/id #uuid "7cda832a-8372-5843-9090-ff689f70dcc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503237} {:answer/id #uuid "abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503326} {:answer/id #uuid "f382cd46-5a63-5f00-8839-d2b57a0f4eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abe1ba41-9a82-5335-848f-464149f07e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503326} :answer-field/id #uuid "270268cf-3633-5ce9-82a2-e7b317c9ea4f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13fcbe15-014a-517d-90d2-a926dca99952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503023} {:answer/id #uuid "5e08c2f6-3dfa-5bb3-a719-57ef08bb49d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503164} {:answer/id #uuid "aebbb419-276a-5105-8b5b-cf284740d9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503335} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9e1839-7886-503f-b4a7-91635be110b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13fcbe15-014a-517d-90d2-a926dca99952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503023} :answer-field/id #uuid "38fcdd80-1693-5154-8b83-577460a5519c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73877eb0-ddb0-5597-a323-c722891a5c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503214} {:answer/id #uuid "77d1819e-5792-5384-8d0c-09042ec44dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503222} {:answer/id #uuid "9b88ea2a-ab65-5102-82bd-5de2dfbfe4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503292} {:answer/id #uuid "c0daeaf8-6af2-5aef-b776-f3a10616640e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503367} {:answer/id #uuid "fc62aa77-dee4-5461-a68f-f82d14f1836d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b88ea2a-ab65-5102-82bd-5de2dfbfe4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503292} :answer-field/id #uuid "81614ff3-0cbe-52bd-8674-7e06ead3791c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f37a13c-db81-5c51-b1fe-cf49ee77cc51" :question/math-academy-id "q-352901" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-x})}^{′}+(u{e}^{-x}) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-x}-u{e}^{-x}+u{e}^{-x} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-x}-\\cancel{u{e}^{-x}}+\\cancel{u{e}^{-x}} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-x} & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\int 3{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
